PART 2 — DATA, MODELS, AND OPERATIONAL ARTIFACTS (PROPRIETARY, ALL RIGHTS RESERVED)
================================================================================

The following material in this repository is PROPRIETARY and NOT covered by the
MIT license above. All rights are reserved by Live Fish Edge / DataNinjaAI.

A. DATA LAYER
   - All .json, .nc, .png, and .bin files under /data/
   - All rasterized oceanographic, atmospheric, and bathymetric products
   - All derivative products (chlorophyll-a, sea surface temperature, currents,
     thermal fronts, chlorophyll fronts, bathymetry, etc.)
   - All grid metadata (bbox, ny/nx, axis definitions)
   - All index files (index.json, index-usec_*.json, sync_manifest.json)

   You may VIEW this data via the live website at https://livefishedge.github.io/
   for personal, non-commercial evaluation. You may NOT:
   - Scrape, bulk-download, mirror, or republish this data
   - Use this data to train, validate, or fine-tune any machine-learning model
   - Use this data in a commercial product or service
   - Redistribute derived or transformed versions of this data

B. ML MODELS AND MODEL OUTPUTS
   - All model weights, checkpoints, and training artifacts
   - All model-produced rasters, composites, and inferences
   - All model-version identifiers, normalizers, feature contracts, and
     inference logic

C. OPERATIONAL ARTIFACTS
   - Pipeline orchestration code (previously in /pipelines/, now in the
     private operations repository)
   - Publish / sanitize scripts
   - Region definitions, retention policies, model-version whitelists
   - Cron jobs, lock files, state files, log files
   - Diagnostic screenshots and internal QA artifacts

